{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For HaShem's portion is His people.</b> For the blessed El has no portion in the human species except His people, for all other nations are estranged from El. And so it is explained that were it not for His people, who were destined then to emerge from those nations, He would have destroyed them in the matter of the dispersion." "<b>Jacob, the cord of His inheritance.</b> For he and his sons are servants to the exalted El; but among the nations of the world, even if some pious man is found among them, this does not carry through to his sons."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Reading בְּעִנְיַן הַפְּלָגָה as 'in the matter of the dispersion,' likely referring to the Tower of Babel narrative."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:56.311436100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}